From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 10:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: exynos9820: Add the host controller driver

The Wi-Fi chip of the boards built around this SoC hangs off the first of
its two PCIe controllers, and nothing in tree drives either of them.

What is taken from the Exynos5433 driver next door is the interrupt and
LTSSM block of ELBI, whose offsets match this controller down to the word.
What is not taken is the reset path: the four reset registers that driver
uses do not exist here, one of them is a read-only interrupt register on
this SoC, and the core reset of this one is a single register at 0x1d0.
Those come from the vendor power sequences, as do the two calibration
tables of the PHY.

The PHY is part of this driver rather than a driver of its own, because
its three resets are registers of the controller, pulsed in the middle of
writing the tables.

The link history the controller keeps, thirty two states deep, is exposed
through debugfs: when a link does not come up, that register block is the
only place that says how far the training got.

Not measured yet: no board in tree enables this controller, and the phone
this was written for has not been flashed with it.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
